  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin prism of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;and refractive index for yellow light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub></mfenced><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is combined with another prism of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn></math>. The combination produces no dispersion. The net average deviation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#948;</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;produced by the combination is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cbfce54d-a710-4902-bbf3-af235dd83a3d-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 179px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula for deviation due to a thin prism is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Therefore, for prism&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>And for prism&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
